# .maroonignore — paths Maroon Elephant skips when scanning THIS repo.
# Glob patterns, gitignore-ish. A directory excludes everything under it.

# Intentionally-vulnerable test fixtures and the test corpus are not product source
# (they deliberately contain the patterns the scanner looks for).
benchmarks/fixtures
tests

# Prose research/spec docs and generated site/docs (not code under analysis).
Findings.md
Build Plan.md
site
docs

# The knowledge pack is pure DATA that enumerates every attack pattern/keyword the scanner
# looks for, so pattern-based rules match it by construction (the classic "scanning the
# scanner" false positive). Excluding the data is standard practice (cf. Semgrep's
# .semgrepignore). Note: the ENGINE source (analyzer.py, taint.py, detect.py, ingest.py, …)
# is NOT excluded — it is scanned, and the few genuine pattern-definition lines carry an
# inline `# maroon: ignore[...]` with a reason, so the dogfood covers the real code.
maroon/knowledge
